-**Parameters:**
-- `N_samples`: Number of coarse samples to infer accumulated opacity. Default: 64 [S1, unofficial].
-- `N_importance`: Number of fine samples to infer accumulated opacity. Default: 64 [S1, unofficial].
-- `chunk`: Chunk size to split input rays to avoid Out Of Memory (OOM). Default: 32*1024 [S1, unofficial].
-- `N_grid`: Size of the 3D grid on one side for querying sigma. Larger values yield higher resolution. Default: 256 [S1, unofficial].
-- `sigma_threshold`: Threshold value for Marching Cubes to consider a location occupied. Default: 20.0 [S1, unofficial].
-- `occ_threshold`: Threshold to consider a vertex occluded. Values larger than this result in fewer occluded pixels. Default: 0.2 [S1, unofficial].
-- `near_t`: Near bound factor to start the ray when using vertex normals. Default: 1.0 [S1, unofficial].
-
-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Precision:** Clamping $\sigma$ to non-negative is critical to prevent invalid Marching Cubes results [S1, unofficial].
-- **Boundaries:** Vertices projected outside image bounds must be discarded or handled to avoid interpolation errors [S1, unofficial].
-- **Occlusion:** Incorrect occlusion estimation leads to dark or ghostly colors. The `occ_threshold` filters out pixels where the NeRF predicts the vertex is behind other geometry [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory:** Large `N_grid` or many training views can cause OOM. Use `chunk` and pixel chunking (30,000) to manage memory [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Subtopics
 
 ### TSDF Estimation via NeRF Occupancy
-A method to estimate the Truncated Signed Distance Field (TSDF) by exploiting NeRF occupancy aggregated along rays to determine points inside and outside the surface [S3]. It computes the median depth $\hat{z}_{i,p,50}$ (first index where accumulated transmittance > 50%) and estimates points outside the surface at the 16th percentile $\hat{z}_{i,p,16}$ and inside at the 84th percentile $\hat{z}_{i,p,84}$ [S3]. These 3D points are fed into a Signed Distance Approximation Network (SSAN) $\phi$ to estimate SDFs, normals, and features: $[\hat{t}_{50}, \hat{n}_{50}, \hat{f}_{50}] = \phi(r_{i,p}(\hat{z}_{i,p,50}))$, $[\hat{t}_{16}, \hat{n}_{16}, \hat{f}_{16}] = \phi(r_{i,p}(\hat{z}_{i,p,16}))$, $[\hat{t}_{84}, \hat{n}_{84}, \hat{f}_{84}] = \phi(r_{i,p}(\hat{z}_{i,p,84}))$ [S3].
+A method to estimate the Truncated Signed Distance Field (TSDF) by exploiting NeRF occupancy aggregated along rays to determine points inside and outside the surface [S3]. It computes the median depth $\hat{z}_{i,p,50}$ as the first index where accumulated transmittance $T_k > 50/100$. It estimates points outside the surface by rendering depth at the 16th percentile $\hat{z}_{i,p,16}$ and inside at the 84th percentile $\hat{z}_{i,p,84}$ [S3]. These 3D coordinates are fed into an SSAN $\phi$ to estimate SDFs, normals, and features: $[\hat{t}_{50}, \hat{n}_{50}, \hat{f}_{50}] = \phi(r_{i,p}(\hat{z}_{i,p,50}))$, $[\hat{t}_{16}, \hat{n}_{16}, \hat{f}_{16}] = \phi(r_{i,p}(\hat{z}_{i,p,16}))$, $[\hat{t}_{84}, \hat{n}_{84}, \hat{f}_{84}] = \phi(r_{i,p}(\hat{z}_{i,p,84}))$ [S3].
