+### Nerfacto Point Cloud Extraction (Depth-based)
+A method to extract 3D geometry from a NeRF by rendering depth maps and back-projecting them, used for real-world unbounded scenes [S4]. It renders depth maps for each input image using the expected ray termination in the density field and back-projects points to 3D coordinates using estimated camera poses [S4]. It uses a small neural network with hash encoding for computational efficiency [S4].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Dominated by the NeRF queries. Density query is $O(N^3)$ [G]. Color fusion is $O(V \cdot M)$ where $M$ is the number of training views [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(N^3)$ for the density grid and $O(V \cdot M)$ for intermediate color accumulation buffers [S1, unofficial].
-- **Performance:** High resolution requires large $N_{grid}$, increasing memory usage quadratically/cubically. Color fusion is slower than vertex normal shading due to multiple view projections and occlusion queries [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Produces textured meshes with consistent colors across views. Handles complex geometry well via Marching Cubes [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Sensitive to $\sigma_{threshold}$. Color artifacts if occlusion is poorly estimated [S1, unofficial]. Not suitable for real-time extraction without optimization [S1, unofficial].
-- **When to use:** When a textured mesh is required from a NeRF and single-view shading is insufficient [S1, unofficial].
-- **When not to use:** When real-time extraction is needed or when the NeRF density field is noisy/unreliable [S1, unofficial].
+- **Time Complexity:** Dominated by the NeRF queries for density ($O(N_{grid}^3)$) and color fusion ($O(N_{vertices} \times N_{views} \times N_{samples})$). The chunking strategy mitigates memory usage but increases I/O overhead.
+- **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing the density grid ($N_{grid}^3$) and intermediate ray marching results. The `chunk` parameter (default 32*1024) controls peak GPU memory [S1, unofficial].
+- **Performance:** $N_{grid}=256$ provides a balance between resolution and computation time [S1, unofficial]. $\sigma_{threshold}=20.0$ is a typical value for occupancy [S1, unofficial].
+- **Strengths:** Produces watertight meshes with consistent colors by leveraging multiple views.
+- **Limitations:** Computationally expensive due to volumetric sampling and multiple NeRF queries. Sensitive to the choice of $\sigma_{threshold}$ and $occ_{threshold}$ [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-Originating from the `nerf_pl` repository [S1, unofficial], this method extends the basic NeRF mesh extraction pipeline by adding a robust color assignment strategy. It addresses the limitation of basic extraction which often results in untextured or poorly colored meshes [S1, unofficial]. The color fusion approach aggregates multi-view information to ensure color consistency [S1, unofficial]. The TSDF variant [S3] further refines geometry by using NeRF occupancy to supervise a signed distance field, improving mesh quality.
+This method originates from the `nerf_pl` repository, which implements NeRF in PyTorch Lightning [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the foundational NeRF paper [S2] by adding mesh extraction and color fusion capabilities. The color fusion technique addresses the view-dependent nature of NeRF colors by aggregating information from all training views [S1, unofficial].
 
